            "tool_use_result": {
              "filePath": "/Users/brenna/.claude/plans/wise-sprouting-music.md",
              "oldString": "Also remove the `bar_clone()` public method if it's only used by the now-removed `progress_bar()`. Check for other callers first.",
              "newString": "Also remove the `bar_clone()` public method \u2014 it has zero callers outside `spinner.rs`.",
              "originalFile": "# Decouple Runner from UI Implementation Details\n\n## Context\n\nThe `SpinnerHandle` trait in `src/ui/mod.rs:177-198` exposes `fn progress_bar(&self) -> Option<ProgressBar>`, leaking the `indicatif::ProgressBar` type through the trait boundary. The runner (`src/runner/workflow.rs:596-633`) uses this to manually construct a live output callback \u2014 knowledge that belongs in the UI layer, not the orchestrator.\n\nThis means:\n- `src/ui/mod.rs` imports `indicatif::ProgressBar` (line 48) just for the trait definition\n- The runner imports `live_output_callback` from `ui::spinner` (line 19) and knows how to wire it up\n- `MockSpinner` returns `None` from `progress_bar()`, so the live output path is untestable in mock scenarios\n\nThe prompts are already properly abstracted via `UserInterface::prompt()` \u2014 no changes needed there.\n\n## Approach\n\nReplace `SpinnerHandle::progress_bar()` with `create_output_callback()` that encapsulates callback creation inside each spinner implementation.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/ui/mod.rs` | Replace `progress_bar()` method, remove `indicatif` import |\n| `src/ui/spinner.rs` | Implement `create_output_callback()` on `ProgressSpinner`, move logic from free fn |\n| `src/ui/non_interactive.rs` | Implement `create_output_callback()` on `NoopSpinner` (returns `None`) |\n| `src/ui/mock.rs` | Implement `create_output_callback()` on `MockSpinner` (returns `None`) |\n| `src/runner/workflow.rs` | Simplify: ask spinner for callback instead of building it manually |\n\n## Detailed Changes\n\n### 1. `src/ui/mod.rs` \u2014 Update `SpinnerHandle` trait\n\nRemove:\n```rust\nuse indicatif::ProgressBar;\n```\n\nReplace `progress_bar()` with:\n```rust\nfn create_output_callback(\n    &self,\n    base_message: String,\n    indent: usize,\n    max_lines: usize,\n) -> Option<crate::shell::OutputCallback> {\n    None\n}\n```\n\n### 2. `src/ui/spinner.rs` \u2014 Implement on `ProgressSpinner`\n\nImplement `create_output_callback` on `ProgressSpinner` by moving the existing `live_output_callback` logic into the method (clone internal `ProgressBar` and build the callback). The existing `live_output_callback` free function stays as-is for the tests, but is no longer called from the runner.\n\nKeep the `live_output_callback` free function (it's tested and useful internally), but `ProgressSpinner::create_output_callback()` will call it:\n```rust\nfn create_output_callback(&self, base_message: String, indent: usize, max_lines: usize) -> Option<OutputCallback> {\n    Some(live_output_callback(self.bar.clone(), base_message, indent, max_lines))\n}\n```\n\nRemove `progress_bar()` override from `ProgressSpinner` (the default `None` return is gone from the trait, so just remove it).\n\nAlso remove the `bar_clone()` public method if it's only used by the now-removed `progress_bar()`. Check for other callers first.\n\n### 3. `src/ui/non_interactive.rs` \u2014 No changes needed\n\n`NoopSpinner` already inherits the default `None` from the trait.\n\n### 4. `src/ui/mock.rs` \u2014 No changes needed\n\n`MockSpinner` already inherits the default `None` from the trait.\n\n### 5. `src/runner/workflow.rs` \u2014 Simplify callback creation\n\nRemove:\n```rust\nuse crate::ui::spinner::live_output_callback;\n```\n\nReplace the manual callback construction (lines 601-633):\n```rust\nlet output_callback = spinner\n    .progress_bar()\n    .and_then(|bar| { ... })\n    .or_else(|| { ... });\n```\n\nWith:\n```rust\nlet output_mode = ui.output_mode();\nlet output_callback = spinner\n    .create_output_callback(\n        attempt_label.clone(),\n        6,\n        match output_mode {\n            OutputMode::Verbose => 3,\n            OutputMode::Normal => 2,\n            _ => 0,\n        },\n    )\n    .or_else(|| {\n        // Non-interactive verbose: stream output directly to stdout\n        if output_mode == OutputMode::Verbose {\n            ... existing fallback ...\n        } else {\n            None\n        }\n    });\n```\n\nThe `or_else` fallback for non-interactive verbose stdout streaming stays because it's a runner-level concern (deciding how non-interactive verbose output works), not a spinner concern. But the spinner-specific callback creation is now fully encapsulated.\n\n### 6. Update tests\n\n- `src/ui/spinner.rs`: Update `progress_bar_returns_clone` and `hidden_spinner_progress_bar_returns_some` tests to test `create_output_callback` instead. The `live_output_callback_*` tests remain unchanged.\n- `src/runner/workflow.rs`: Existing integration tests should pass unchanged since behavior is identical.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ncargo test --all-features\ncargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\ncargo fmt -- --check\ncargo doc --no-deps --all-features\ncargo build --all-targets --all-features\n```\n",
              "structuredPatch": [
